<description>
The `Arg()` helper has many benefits:

* It does not require manual `isNull` checks
* It does not require hard-coding the fallback/default value a second time
* It does not require manually specifying the getter for the type. Specifying the type is enough.

So use it more broadly.
</description>

<commits>
fae108b0a2 rpc: Use the first arg name in GetParamIndex

GetName does not support aliases at all. However, it should be fine for
GetParamIndex (used in Arg and MaybeArg) to support lookup by the first
name.

The test is modified to show the second legacy alias is ignored.

faf064078b rpc: doc: Use proper RPCArg::Default in verifychain

fae633e268 refactor: rpc: Use self.Arg<_>(name) helper over manual isNull() ? fallback : getter()

The Arg() helper has many benefits:

* It does not require manual isNull checks
* It does not require hard-coding the fallback/default value a second time
* It does not require manually specifying the getter for the type. Specifying the type is enough.

So use it in this refactor, which does not change any behavior.

fa77e12603 doc: Fix typo in walletcreatefundedpsbt dev comment

Use same wording as in walletprocesspsbt
</commits>

